  "comment": "Jerome's Chronicon entry and the Aristides chapter of De viris illustribus are the two S passages; Jerome's own chapter 19 body on Quadratus (not among the supplied contexts) is also S. Jerome treats Quadratus as bishop of Athens; NPNF note says 'not the Athenian bishop'. I took the hits as the apologist who presented a work to Hadrian."
